# The <ay-init-msg> golden fixture is asserted BYTE FOR BYTE against both
# runtimes — ts/initMsg.spec.ts reads it with readFileSync, rs/src/init_msg.rs
# embeds it with include_str! — so an agent cannot tell which runtime launched
# it from the shape of its own prompt. That only holds if the file's bytes are
# identical on every platform. Git's autocrlf (on by default for the Windows CI
# runners) otherwise rewrites the LFs to CRLF at checkout, and the parity test
# fails on windows-latest while passing everywhere else.
tests/fixtures/*.golden.txt text eol=lf
